### Base URL variable
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@clusterId = 1


### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — fully automatic (weather + temporal from server)
# Weather is fetched from Open-Meteo using the cluster centroid.
# Temporal features (hour, is_night, is_weekend …) are derived from the server clock.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — override weather condition only
# Road surface and road condition are derived from the provided weather.
# Temporal features are still taken from the server clock.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}?weather_condition=rain

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — override all weather conditions (skips Open-Meteo)
# When weather_condition is provided, Open-Meteo is not called.
# light_condition is still derived from the server clock if omitted.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}?weather_condition=snow&road_surface=ice&road_condition=slippery

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — specify full conditions including light
# All weather fields provided → fully user-controlled, no external API call.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}?weather_condition=fog&road_surface=wet&light_condition=dark&road_condition=reduced_visibility

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — add accident type and cause hints
# accident_type and cause_primary are optional model hints.
# They default to "unknown" when omitted.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}?weather_condition=clear&road_surface=dry&accident_type=collision&cause_primary=speed

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — clear summer day scenario
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}?weather_condition=clear&road_surface=dry&light_condition=daylight&road_condition=normal

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — worst-case winter night scenario
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}?weather_condition=snow&road_surface=ice&light_condition=dark&road_condition=slippery

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — 404 cluster not found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/99999

###

### GET /api/prediction/clusters/{id} — 503 models not loaded
# Returned when scripts/train_model.py has not been run yet (no .joblib files in models/).
# Example only — expects 503 if models directory is empty.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prediction/clusters/{{clusterId}}
